      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Extra Information:

    In this recipe, sodium tends to run high due to
    soy sauce (up to 600

    mg- 900 mg of sodium).

    Culinary History: Initially
    introduced by Hokkien-speaking Chinese

    migrants and traders who introduced
    noodles to the Philippine islands. The

    dish evolved with local ingredients
    and techniques and is a common

    everyday meal. Pancit carries a superstition
    still observed today; not to cut

    the noodles as long strands are believed
    to symbolise a long life which is

    why this dish is popular at Filipino birthdays.'
